---
<GuideLayout title="Intermediate 2.6 · The 70s: Song of the Elves Preparation" current="intermediate">
  <div class="page-grid">
    <aside class="sidebar"><IntermediateNav current="2-6" /></aside>
    <article class="content">
      <header class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-kicker">Intermediate · Chapter 2.6</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">The 70s: Song of the Elves Preparation</h1>
        <p class="chapter-summary">Work toward the eight skills needed for Song of the Elves, using quest rewards to shorten the training. Switch between Sailing, Ranged and Hunter when you want a change of pace, while Farming and kingdom herbs keep growing in the background.</p>
      </header>

      <ChapterGoals
        summary="Reach unboosted 70 in all eight Song of the Elves skills; complete the useful quest chain and prepare the 2.7 elf finale."
        stats={["Unboosted 70 Agility, Construction, Farming, Herblore", "Unboosted 70 Hunter, Mining, Smithing, Woodcutting", "60 Ranged; 67 Sailing; 71 Mining for the dwarven-stout boost"]}
        unlocks={["Ava's accumulator; full Fairytale II; Weiss herb patch", "The Red Reef, Sacred Grove and a camphor-hulled skiff", "Dream Mentor, Defender of Varrock and Making History complete"]}
      />

      <div class="callout"><strong>Before you begin:</strong> complete Sins of the Father and Troubled Tortugans and unlock Piety in 2.5. Check your skills and banked herbs, teaks, metal and minigame points before gathering more supplies. Train only as much as you still need at each step. Temporary boosts help with Making Friends, but all eight Song of the Elves skills must reach 70 without boosts.</div>

      <section><div class="section-label">Background training</div><h2>Keep Farming and kingdom resources going when convenient.</h2></section>
      <div class="callout"><strong>Farming:</strong> Continue Chapter 1.4's tree and fruit-tree routine, occasional Fossil Island hardwoods, herb runs and accessible Farming Contracts when convenient. Your Farming level depends on how many runs you have done. Check for 49 before finishing Fairytale II below, then reach <strong>unboosted 70 before Song of the Elves</strong>. Use the active training options below if you want to finish the remaining levels sooner. Add the disease-free Weiss herb patch after Making Friends. <strong>Birdhouses:</strong> do them when convenient, and use the Hunter training steps below for any remaining levels. <strong>Managing Miscellania:</strong> keep the treasury funded and approval reasonable. Stay herb-heavy; put the other workers on teaks while Construction still needs planks, then move them to maples for nests/seeds or coal for Smithing according to your bank. There is no daily-collection requirement.</div>

      <section><div class="section-label">Close old quest threads</div><h2>Finish three stories that help with the later quests.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i26-icthlarin" number="1" title="Complete Icthlarin's Little Helper for Agility XP">
        <p>Take a cat or kitten from Gertrude's Cat, food, combat gear and desert access via Shantay Pass. <strong>Bank check:</strong> one bucket of sap, one willow log, one bag of salt, a <strong>full waterskin(4)</strong>, tinderbox and at least 600 coins; take extra waterskins for travel so the hand-in one stays full. The Wanderer west of the Agility Pyramid, north of Sophanem draws you into hypnotised pyramid passages, then Sophanem's priest and carpenter send you through the burial preparations. The pyramid has traps and combat; bank between phases if needed and use the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Icthlarin%27s_Little_Helper" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">quest map</a> for the hypnotised sequence. Completion opens <strong>Sophanem and its carpet connection</strong> and gives <strong>4,500 Thieving, 4,000 Agility and 4,000 Woodcutting XP</strong>. Check your new Agility level afterward.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Replace the burial supplies before the desert trip">
          <p>Check whether you still have the bucket of sap collected in Chapter 1. Use a <strong>knife on an evergreen tree with an empty bucket</strong> to collect another bucket of sap; the evergreens outside Falador work. Cut a willow log at Draynor, buy <strong>one bag of salt from a Slayer master</strong>, and buy full waterskins/desert clothing at Shantay Pass. A knife spawns in Lumbridge Castle's kitchen, and its general store supplies a bucket and tinderbox.</p>
          <p>Buy <strong>linen from Raetul in eastern Sophanem for 30 coins</strong> when the burial preparation needs it. The 600-coin travel/payment buffer covers this; linen is a quest purchase, not ordinary cloth or silk. Bring your living cat/kitten; if missing, buy another kitten from Gertrude for 100 coins. Use the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}>prayer and antipoison recovery</a> if the bank has no doses.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-tail" number="2" title="Complete A Tail of Two Cats; use both lamps on Herblore">
        <p>With your cat and catspeak amulet, start at <strong>Unferth in east Burthorpe</strong>. Hild can enchant the amulet for five death runes: its whiskers then work like a compass to locate roaming Bob. His exact position changes, so use the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/A_Tail_of_Two_Cats" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">current Bob-location guide</a> rather than a fixed coordinate. <strong>Bank check:</strong> five death runes, one whole chocolate cake, one ordinary log, tinderbox, bucket of milk, shears, <strong>four potato seeds</strong>, rake, seed dibber, vial of water, desert shirt and desert robe. The potato patch grows while you do the other parts. The quest closes direct future <strong>While Guthix Sleeps</strong> and <strong>Dragon Slayer II</strong> prerequisites without a new skill grind. Put <strong>both 2,500-XP lamps into Herblore</strong>.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Prepare Unferth's food, seeds and disguise">
          <p>At <strong>50 Cooking</strong>, use a chocolate bar on a <strong>whole cake</strong> to make the chocolate cake. Steal the cake from an Ardougne cake stall and buy the chocolate bar and milk from the Culinaromancer's Chest; a part-eaten cake is not the hand-in. Buy the five death runes from Aubury.</p>
          <p>Buy <strong>four potato seeds from Olivia in Draynor</strong>, and missing rake/dibber from Sarah's Farming shop south of Falador. Shantay sells the <strong>desert shirt and desert robe</strong>; bring these exact two pieces for the disguise. Jatix supplies the vial of water. Cut the log and replace shears/tinderbox at Lumbridge's general store.</p>
          <p>If the <strong>catspeak amulet</strong> was lost, ask the <strong>Sphinx in Sophanem</strong> for another; recover a kitten from Gertrude if needed. The quest provides the doctor/nurse hat during its disguise sequence, so there is no outside hat purchase.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-fairytale" number="3" title="Finish Fairytale II; put its lamp into Herblore">
        <p>In Chapter 1, you stopped once fairy rings were unlocked. Now check <strong>unboosted 40 Thieving, 49 Farming and 57 Herblore</strong>. If passive Farming is still below 49, continue the available tree/fruit-tree circuit or use Tithe Farm to finish the remaining XP; <strong>reach unboosted 49 Farming before continuing the quest</strong>. Then resume from the point where you unlocked fairy rings. Carry a dramen/lunar staff, vial of water, pestle and mortar, food and a suitable weapon. Follow Nuff's certificate/ring sequence, recover the Queen's secateurs, then gather star flower and a Gorak claw for the magic essence potion. <strong>Goraks ignore protection prayers</strong>; bring food and consider safespotting rather than relying on Prayer. Full completion gives <strong>3,500 Herblore XP</strong> and a selectable <strong>2,500-XP lamp for Herblore</strong>, and completes the quest requirement for a future POH fairy ring. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Fairytale_II_-_Cure_a_Queen" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest guide</a>.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Recover the certificate and make this quest's own potion">
          <p>Search <strong>Fairy Nuff's room in north-west Zanaris</strong> for another Nuff's certificate if it is no longer banked, and read it before repeating the ring-code sequence. A missing dramen staff can be remade with the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-4/#i24-lunar`}>Lunar preparation's Entrana method</a>; buy a vial of water and pestle and mortar from Jatix.</p>
          <p>The potion ingredients are <strong>quest-local</strong>: pick a star flower on the <strong>CKP</strong> plane when it grows, and obtain a claw from a Gorak on <strong>DIR</strong>. At 57 Herblore, put the star flower in the vial of water and add the claw crushed with the pestle and mortar. This is <strong>magic essence</strong>, not a potion made from the ordinary herb stock.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Ranged · first half</div><h2>Get Ava's accumulator and a quest lamp before training to 60.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i26-ranged-50" number="4" title="Reach 50 Ranged, then pause">
        <p>Mourning's End Part I eventually needs <strong>unboosted 60 Ranged</strong>, but do not do the whole gap at once. Check your level after the earlier quest rewards; train only to <strong>unboosted 50</strong>. Gemstone Crab in the Tlati Rainforest is a relaxed, long-idle target; Ammonite or Sand Crabs work too. For cheap Ironman ammo, buy a <strong>Dorgeshuun crossbow and bone bolts from Nardok in the Dorgesh-Kaan mine</strong>, accessible after The Lost Tribe; the shop stocks the crossbow and inexpensive bolts/packs. Use the earlier arrow stock instead if preferred. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Nardok%27s_Bone_Weapons" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Shop stock</a>.</p>
        <TrainingOptions id="i26-ranged-methods" informational={true} skill="Ranged" target="50 now, 60 later" why="Reach 50 for Ava's accumulator, then use Dream Mentor's lamp before continuing to the unboostable 60-Ranged requirement." recommended="Gemstone Crab or another low-attention crab with cheap bone bolts." relaxed="Use existing arrows with Ava's attractor if the stock is already convenient." />
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-accumulator" number="5" title="Upgrade Ava's attractor to accumulator">
        <p>At <strong>unboosted 50 Ranged</strong>, return to Ava in Draynor Manor with the <strong>existing attractor and 75 steel arrows</strong>. Upgrade to <strong>Ava's accumulator</strong>; check the bank before paying for a replacement attractor. Equip it for the remaining Ranged work. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Ava%27s_accumulator" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Upgrade requirements</a>.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Recover the device and missing arrows">
          <p>If the arrows were used, buy the shortfall from <strong>Lowe's Archery Emporium in Varrock</strong>. If the attractor itself is missing, bring <strong>999 coins plus 75 steel arrows</strong> to Ava for the accumulator at unboosted 50 Ranged. The retained attractor replaces the 999-coin payment when you still have it.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-dream" number="6" title="Complete Dream Mentor; put the dreamy lamp into Ranged">
        <p>Check Lunar Diplomacy, Eadgar's Ruse and unboosted 85+ combat; check the current goutweed stock. Start with <strong>Cyrisus in the Lunar Isle mine</strong>; <strong>bank check:</strong> seal of passage, <strong>20 pieces of food in three types (7 + 7 + 6)</strong> for Cyrisus, one goutweed, one astral rune, hammer, pestle and mortar, and <strong>tinderbox</strong>. The quest supplies its special dream vial. Rebank into your strongest reliable combat gear and <strong>many high-healing food pieces</strong> before the dream: there are <strong>four consecutive bosses, no Prayer and no emergency teleport</strong>. The dream lectern is the exit if you need to restart. Read each boss's mechanics first and prepare enough food to fight without Prayer. Rewards are <strong>15,000 Hitpoints and 10,000 Magic XP</strong> plus a <strong>15,000-XP dreamy lamp</strong> for a combat skill other than Attack or Prayer. Put that lamp into <strong>Ranged</strong>. This also closes a While Guthix Sleeps prerequisite. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Dream_Mentor" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Boss guide</a>.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Separate Cyrisus's food from the boss inventory">
          <p>Cyrisus needs three distinct food types. For a simple refill, catch/cook <strong>seven salmon, seven tuna and six lobsters</strong>: fly-fish salmon at Lumbridge/Shilo and fish the sea types at Catherby with a harpoon and lobster pot from Gerrant. Cook until the required <em>successful</em> counts are banked. Use other suitable banked food types if you already have them; keep your high-healing boss food separate.</p>
          <p>If Eadgar's Ruse used the last <strong>goutweed</strong>, steal another from the <strong>Troll Stronghold kitchen storeroom</strong> using its guard-avoidance route. This is not a gout tuber. Buy the astral rune from <strong>Baba Yaga on Lunar Isle</strong>, and ask Brundt in Rellekka for a replacement seal of passage. Fill the <strong>quest-provided dream vial</strong> and follow the goutweed/ground-astral sequence; an ordinary shop vial does not replace it.</p>
          <p>Before entering the dream, refill high-healing food with the established Tai Bwo Wannai karambwan fishing/cooking loop. There is no prayer-potion requirement for the dream itself because Prayer is disabled; the four-boss food supply must survive that sequence.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Making Friends · spend the rewards early</div><h2>Use two reliable boosts to claim the quest XP sooner.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i26-agility-65" number="7" title="Reach 65 Agility and prepare an Agility potion">
        <p>Check your Agility level after Icthlarin's Little Helper. At the <strong>Colossal Wyrm Remains in Varlamore's Avium Savannah</strong>, continue the basic course until <strong>unboosted 62</strong>, then use its advanced course through <strong>unboosted 65</strong>. Its longer obstacle animations make it a lower-input option; Seers rooftops are an alternative <strong>once unboosted 60 is reached</strong>; use Falador rooftops before that if you prefer them. Hallowed Sepulchre, unlocked by Sins, is an optional, more active method. <strong>Check your remaining Agility-potion doses:</strong> use the four-dose bottle reserved during Tai Bwo Wannai Trio preparation if it remains, or refill the shortfall through 2.4's <strong>Brimhaven Agility Arena toadflax</strong> (three vouchers per herb), vial of water and <strong>Gnome Stronghold swamp toad's legs</strong> recipe. Use banked or farmed toadflax if available; the arena lets you obtain more without waiting for a seed drop or crop. Keep this bottle separate from the one handed to Tamayu during Trio. The potion gives <strong>+3 Agility</strong>, so <strong>65 + 3 = 68</strong> for Making Friends. No Summer pie is required. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Colossal_agility" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Course details</a>.</p>
        <TrainingOptions id="i26-agility-methods" informational={true} skill="Agility" target="65 for the quest, then 70 later" why="The +3 potion reaches the boostable 68 check; Making Friends then awards 50,000 Agility XP." recommended="Basic-to-advanced Colossal Wyrm course at 62, then continue to 65." relaxed="Seers rooftops if you prefer marks of grace." fast="Hallowed Sepulchre if you enjoy a more active obstacle run." />
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-eagles" number="8" title="Complete Eagles' Peak as a quest break">
        <p>Speak to <strong>Charlie at Ardougne Zoo</strong> and follow the eagle-rescue trail to the Piscatoris area. <strong>Bank check:</strong> one yellow dye, one swamp tar and 50 coins, plus food and a teleport. Collect the quest's feathers and puzzle items locally. The quest awards <strong>2,500 Hunter XP</strong>, unlocks <strong>box traps</strong> and enables chinchompa hunting if you want to try it later. This short quest breaks up the two Making Friends skill preparations. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Eagles%27_Peak" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quest guide</a>.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Supply the beak/cape ingredients">
          <p>Make <strong>yellow dye at Aggie in Draynor with two onions and five coins</strong>, or use one still banked. Pick up one swamp tar in Lumbridge Swamp. During the quest collect <strong>ten eagle feathers</strong> in the Eagles' Peak caves; take these, the dye, tar and 50 coins to <strong>Azyff in Varrock's Fancy Clothes Store</strong> for two fake beaks and two eagle capes.</p>
          <p>The metal feather, coloured puzzle feathers, odd bird seed and ferret-catching equipment are supplied in the quest area. The first completion does not require a pre-purchased rope or a stock of Hunter bait.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-mining-71" number="9" title="Reach 71 Mining and buy a dwarven stout">
        <p>Starting from your level after Lunar Diplomacy, train only as much as you still need to <strong>unboosted 71</strong>. Shooting Stars are the relaxed option; Motherlode Mine is the resource-focused option because its ores can feed Smithing. A normal <strong>dwarven stout gives +1 Mining</strong> and can be bought from <strong>the Rising Sun Inn in Falador</strong>; <strong>71 + 1 = 72</strong> at the Making Friends check. This also clears Song of the Elves' unboosted 70 Mining gate. If you strongly prefer avoiding level 71 and accept RNG, unboosted 70 plus a successful +2 orange-spice stew is optional; it is <em>not</em> this route's default. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Temporary_skill_boost" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Boost reference</a>.</p>
        <TrainingOptions id="i26-mining-methods" informational={true} skill="Mining" target="71, unboosted" why="A cheap +1 stout reaches Making Friends' boostable 72 gate without stew RNG." recommended="Shooting Stars for lower attention; stop when your skill tab shows 71." resource="Motherlode Mine when you want ores for the later Smithing work." />
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-friends" number="10" title="Complete Making Friends with My Arm; open Weiss">
        <p>Confirm <strong>unboosted 66 Firemaking</strong> (already exceeded), <strong>35 Construction</strong> (exceeded), and completed <strong>Swan Song, Cold War, My Arm's Big Adventure and Romeo &amp; Juliet</strong> (the last was finished in 1.1). Use the <strong>four-dose Agility potion reserved in 2.4</strong> and bring access to extra <strong>dwarven stouts</strong>; reapply the <strong>65→68 Agility</strong> and <strong>71→72 Mining</strong> boosts when the relevant checks occur. If that potion was spent, repeat 2.4's Brimhaven Arena toadflax + toad's-legs recipe for only the missing doses. Before travelling, check these supplies: <strong>saw, hammer, one bolt of cloth, five mahogany planks and one cadava berry</strong>. If the berry was not banked after Romeo &amp; Juliet, pick one from the <strong>wild cadava bushes directly west of the south-east Varrock mine</strong> before visiting the Varrock Apothecary. Bring combat gear, food, Prayer restores, tinderbox and troll-area travel. A <strong>bucket of water, rope and pickaxe</strong> are also required, but can be obtained during the quest; bring your own to avoid detours. Bank before the fight and follow the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Making_Friends_with_My_Arm" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">current quest/boss guide</a> for the fire-pit and monster mechanics. Claim <strong>50,000 Agility, 50,000 Mining, 40,000 Firemaking and 10,000 Construction XP</strong>. The <strong>disease-free Weiss herb patch</strong> joins your normal herb runs now. Check your new Agility, Mining and Construction levels after claiming the rewards.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Buy new cloth and planks; refill both temporary boosts">
          <p>Buy the <strong>bolt of cloth for 650 coins from the Varrock sawmill operator</strong>. Check for <strong>five mahogany planks still present</strong> after the lectern and Cold War; if short, cut the missing mahogany logs north of the Farming Guild and convert them at a sawmill for <strong>1,500 coins each</strong>. The full five cost 7,500 coins in conversion fees.</p>
          <p>Buy ordinary <strong>dwarven stouts from the Rising Sun Inn in Falador</strong> for the +1 Mining check. The <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-4/#i24-trio`}>Trio preparation</a> gives the repeatable toadflax/toad's-legs recipe for the <strong>Agility potion(4)</strong>. Carry enough doses/drinks to repeat checks if a boost expires; check how many doses remain in your saved bottle.</p>
          <p>Replace hammer/tinderbox/bucket at Lumbridge's general store, saw at the sawmill, rope from Ned, and pickaxe from Nurmof in the Dwarven Mine if needed. Refill combat supplies through the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}>potion supply note</a> before the fight.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Sailing · first return</div><h2>A quest at 52 makes the trip more than a level bar.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i26-sailing-52" number="11" title="Continue Sailing after Troubled Tortugans and reach 52">
        <p>After Troubled Tortugans, use <strong>The Summer Shore notice board</strong> for courier tasks: accept a delivery, pick up the crate at its ledger, put it in your cargo hold, sail to the destination and deposit it at the receiving ledger. Choose available routes rather than forcing one perfect loop. Chart newly reachable water/landmarks for one-time XP and try salvage when you want a change of pace. Bring routine food/repair supplies where your route crosses danger. After claiming Troubled Tortugans' 10,000 XP, continue until the skill tab shows <strong>52 Sailing</strong>. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Sailing_training" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current training guide</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-reef" number="12" title="Complete The Red Reef for Sailing and Smithing XP">
        <p>Check <strong>unboosted 52 Sailing and 48 Smithing</strong>, plus Troubled Tortugans. Begin with the Tortugans at <strong>The Summer Shore/Great Conch</strong>. Equip the boat with working cannons and ammunition <em>or</em> suitable Magic/Ranged gear to attack the pirate crews; bring <strong>repair kits covering at least roughly 300 boat hitpoints</strong>, food, protection-prayer supplies and land-combat gear. The quest includes two hostile pirate boats, pirates on land and later bosses. <strong>Protect from Missiles</strong> helps against ship captains, and bank/regear before the island fights. Boat <em>capsizing</em> is not a Hardcore death, but your character reaching zero Hitpoints aboard or on an island is an unsafe death; HCIM should not treat this as a harmless minigame. Read the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/The_Red_Reef" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">quest combat guide</a> before the instanced fight. Claim <strong>15,000 Sailing and 5,000 Smithing XP</strong>, <strong>Sacred Grove/camphor resources</strong> and the <strong>Bosun's Bench schematic</strong>. Check your Smithing level before the training to 55 and 70 below.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Refill repair kits and combat supplies before sailing out">
          <p>The Magic/Ranged crew-kill route avoids needing a cannon upgrade or cannonball stock. Use the combat equipment you already own. The quest supplies the <strong>deep sea helmet and apparatus</strong> for its dive; these are not the earlier RFD diving items.</p>
          <p>For the roughly 300-boat-HP reserve, make <strong>ten mahogany repair kits</strong> (30 repair each) at a <strong>shipwright's workbench</strong>, using its mahogany-kit recipe; your unboosted 62+ Construction clears the 47 requirement. Bring hammer and saw. Refill the recipe's <strong>mahogany planks</strong> by cutting logs north of the Farming Guild and paying a sawmill 1,500 coins each; make <strong>mithril nails</strong> at an anvil from mithril bars (Ordan's mithril ore plus four coal per bar), and buy <strong>swamp paste from Shipwright Seb or the Port Khazard general store</strong>. Make only the missing repair kits, checking the workbench's required quantities before buying a batch.</p>
          <p>Repair kits heal the boat, not your character. Bank fresh food and <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}>prayer potions</a> for the land fights as a separate supply check.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Hunter and Smithing · useful interim stops</div><h2>Let Defender's rewards reduce both later grinds.</h2></section>

      <RouteStep id="i26-hunter-52" number="13" title="Check your Hunter level and train to 52">
        <p>Check the skill tab after Eagles' Peak and any birdhouses. For more Hunter XP now, travel to the <strong>Hunter Guild in Varlamore</strong> and speak to <strong>Guild Scribe Verity in the Burrow</strong>. At unboosted 46, Huntmaster Gilman gives <strong>Novice Hunters' Rumours</strong>: receive an assigned creature, bring the normal trap/tools for it, hunt until its rare part appears, then return it for Hunter XP and a loot sack. Assignments and rare-part timing vary; consult the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Hunters%27_Rumours" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">creature/trap reference</a> as needed, to find the tools for each assignment. Work with the assignments you receive and check your level between rumours. Stop temporarily at <strong>unboosted 52</strong> for Defender.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-smithing-55" number="14" title="Reach 55 Smithing before Defender of Varrock">
        <p>After claiming The Red Reef's <strong>5,000 Smithing XP</strong>, check your skill tab. Use <strong>Giants' Foundry</strong> for the resource-efficient default: bring banked metal bars to the foundry south of Al Kharid, cast a sword in the mould, then work its heat/shape stations as the progress markers direct. Use banked-bar smithing for a simpler anvil loop, or Blast Furnace gold with the Family Crest <strong>goldsmith gauntlets</strong> if you want a faster active alternative and have ore. Stop at <strong>unboosted 55</strong>; Defender then gives 15,000 more XP. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Giants%27_Foundry" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Foundry primer</a>.</p>
        <TrainingOptions id="i26-smithing-methods" informational={true} skill="Smithing" target="55 now, 70 after Defender" why="Spend the quest's 15,000 XP before paying for the final stretch." recommended="Giants' Foundry from available metal bars." relaxed="Ordinary bar smithing at an anvil." fast="Blast Furnace gold with goldsmith gauntlets if you have the resources." />
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-rc-35" number="15" title="Check for 35 Runecraft before What Lies Below">
        <p>The quests completed so far award <strong>1,000 Enter the Abyss + 6,000 The Eyes of Glouphrie + 500 The Ascent of Arceuus + 5,000 Lunar Diplomacy + 9,210 Temple of the Eye + 3,500 The Slug Menace = 25,210 Runecraft XP</strong>, before any other Runecraft training. Level 35 starts at <strong>22,406 XP</strong> and level 36 at <strong>24,742 XP</strong>, so these rewards bring you to <strong>at least 36</strong>, enough for What Lies Below's 35 requirement. Check your skill tab. If it shows less than 35, make sure each listed quest is complete and its rewards claimed. Use a few Guardians of the Rift rounds for any remaining XP, stopping at 35.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-what" number="16" title="Complete What Lies Below">
        <p>With <strong>unboosted 35 Runecraft</strong>, speak to <strong>Rat Burgiss south of Varrock</strong>. Bring a chaos talisman/tiara or use the <strong>Temple of the Eye's Guardian of Chaos</strong> route to the chaos altar; the latter avoids a Wilderness trip. <strong>Bank check:</strong> one <strong>empty bowl</strong> and <strong>15 chaos runes</strong>, plus Varrock travel, food and combat gear. Follow Surok's investigation and the King Roald encounter using the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/What_Lies_Below" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">quest guide</a>. Claim <strong>8,000 Runecraft XP</strong>. This completes the last prerequisite for Defender of Varrock.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Bring the hand-ins and use a supplied altar route">
          <p>Buy <strong>15 chaos runes from Aubury</strong>. Make an empty bowl from one soft clay at the <strong>Rimmington pottery wheel, then fire it in the pottery oven</strong> (8 Crafting); this is a fired bowl, unlike Dragon Slayer's unfired one. Rat and Surok provide the folder, letters and metal wand during their steps.</p>
          <p>At <strong>35 Runecraft</strong>, enter a Guardians of the Rift game and use the active <strong>Guardian of Chaos</strong> portal when it appears. Take Surok's wand and all 15 chaos runes to the altar and charge the wand there. Temple of the Eye is complete, so this route needs no chaos talisman or new Wilderness access; no extra rune essence is needed for the wand charge.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-defender" number="17" title="Complete Defender of Varrock; claim its museum lamp">
        <p>Check <strong>unboosted 55 Smithing and 52 Hunter</strong>. The quest log already contains <strong>Shield of Arrav, Temple of Ikov, Below Ice Mountain, Family Crest, Garden of Tranquillity (and Creature of Fenkenstrain), What Lies Below, Romeo &amp; Juliet, Demon Slayer and Rune Mysteries</strong>. Start with <strong>Elias White at the Jolly Boar Inn</strong>. Take a pickaxe for barronite, teleport options for Varrock/Camdozaal, food, prayer supplies and the retained <strong>Salve amulet</strong> for armoured zombies; the route's Piety/defender kit exceeds the combat recommendation. Follow the tracks, forge work and Varrock defence in the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Defender_of_Varrock" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">quest guide</a>. Claim <strong>15,000 Smithing and 15,000 Hunter XP</strong> and access to <strong>Zemouregal's Base</strong>. At the Varrock Museum, talk to <strong>Historian Minas</strong> for the separate <strong>5,000-XP antique lamp</strong>; put it into <strong>Herblore</strong>. This helps three current 70 grinds and prepares While Guthix Sleeps.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Collect the forge ingredients in Camdozaal">
          <p>No outside bar, ore or gem hand-in is required. The quest supplies its mist bottle and other story items. In <strong>Camdozaal</strong>, mine the required <strong>barronite deposit</strong> and fight a <strong>chaos golem for a chaos core</strong> when instructed, then use the quest's forge process. Bring your pickaxe; Nurmof in the Dwarven Mine sells replacements.</p>
          <p>The retained Salve is recommended combat equipment. If it is missing, use the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-5/#i25-haunted`}>Haunted Mine preparation</a> to replace the crystal and wool, then Tarn's diary for its enchantment. Refill food and <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}>prayer doses</a> before the zombie fights.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <div class="callout"><strong>Save these for Chapter 3:</strong> Path of Glouphrie needs <strong>56 Slayer</strong>; later steps cover that training before While Guthix Sleeps. You can also leave The Curse of Arrav and Mage Arena II until later, including their 62 Ranged and 75 Magic preparation.</div>

      <section><div class="section-label">Construction, then a Sailing break</div><h2>Use the plank sack and check your remaining planks before buying more.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i26-construction-70" number="18" title="Train Construction to 70">
        <p>Check your Construction XP after 2.1's training to at least 62, <strong>Darkness of Hallowvale's 2,000 XP</strong> and <strong>Making Friends' 10,000 XP</strong>. Any additional contracts or shipbuilding will have added more. Use the plank sack and <strong>Adept Mahogany Homes</strong> with kingdom teaks and remaining 2.1 planks first. If neither is stocked, repeat <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-1/#i21-teak-prep`}>2.1's ordinary teak-cutting and sawmill loop</a>; the Castle Wars tree works when Fossil Island trees are unavailable. Refill steel bars from Ordan's iron ore and coal as needed. Starting from level 62, the two named quest rewards leave roughly <strong>390,000 XP</strong> to level 70; at an average around <strong>280 total XP per teak plank</strong> in Adept contracts, roughly <strong>1,400 teaks</strong> gives a rough idea of the amount needed. Starting above 62, varying contracts and banked planks move this substantially: think <strong>roughly 1,000–1,500 teaks total</strong> if you started around 62, and prepare/top up in smaller batches rather than chopping a rigid total. Faster POH furniture uses more planks but remains a choice. Once the remaining plank need is comfortably covered, non-herb kingdom workers can switch to maples or coal. Stop at <strong>unboosted 70</strong>. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Mahogany_Homes" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Contract reference</a>.</p>
        <TrainingOptions id="i26-construction-methods" informational={true} skill="Construction" target="70, unboosted" why="Song of the Elves needs an unboosted 70; check your remaining XP before making more planks." recommended="Adept Mahogany Homes, plank sack, kingdom teaks and regular level checks." fast="POH furniture if you value speed over teak efficiency." />
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-sailing-60" number="19" title="Return to Sailing and pause at 60">
        <p>After claiming The Red Reef's <strong>15,000 Sailing XP</strong>, continue from your new level. Rotate ordinary Summer Shore courier deliveries with new charting and salvage rather than repeating one loop until 67. Stop at <strong>unboosted 60</strong>: camphor-era ship facilities begin to matter around here, and this is a useful pacing break, <em>not</em> a Song of the Elves gate. Keep any camphor gathered in the Sacred Grove for later ship work.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Ranged and Hunter · second half</div><h2>Use the quest rewards to finish the remaining training.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i26-ranged-60" number="20" title="Finish 60 Ranged for Mourning's End Part I">
        <p>Check your Ranged XP after using Dream Mentor's <strong>15,000-XP lamp</strong>. With the accumulator equipped, return to Gemstone/Ammonite/Sand Crabs and train only the remaining gap to <strong>unboosted 60</strong>. The cheap Ironman default is Nardok's <strong>Dorgeshuun crossbow plus bone bolts</strong>; buy bolts/packs in manageable batches as the stack runs down. Existing bows/arrows are fine. Stop at 60, not 62 for the deferred Curse of Arrav.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-hunter-70" number="21" title="Finish 70 Hunter with Hunters' Rumours">
        <p>Check your Hunter XP after Eagles' Peak's <strong>2,500</strong>, Defender's <strong>15,000</strong> and any birdhouse runs you have done. Continue the Hunter Guild loop. At <strong>unboosted 57</strong>, ask Cervus or Ornus for <strong>Adept rumours</strong>; they use the same assigned-creature → rare-part → return loop but a different task pool and better loot sacks. You may keep a comfortable Novice task if preferred. Continue birdhouses when convenient, and use rumours to finish the levels you still need. Stop at <strong>unboosted 70</strong>. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Hunters%27_Rumours" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Rumour tiers</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">A quest before the final training</div><h2>Complete Making History for Song of the Elves.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i26-making-history" number="22" title="Complete Making History and claim the museum lamp">
        <p>Start with <strong>Jorral at the outpost north-west of West Ardougne</strong>. Stage a <strong>spade, <em>unenchanted</em> strung sapphire amulet and ghostspeak amulet</strong>, plus the Ectophial, Rellekka/Ardougne travel and teleports. Ghosts Ahoy already gives free Port Phasmatys entry; so you can enter without paying more ecto-tokens. Follow the three witness stories and enchanted-key clues in the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Making_History" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">quest guide</a>; there is no combat boss. Keep the <strong>enchanted key</strong> if you want its later treasure trail. Completion is a <strong>direct Song of the Elves prerequisite</strong>. Tell <strong>Historian Minas at the Varrock Museum</strong> the history for the separate <strong>1,000-XP lamp</strong> and put it into <strong>Herblore</strong>.</p>
      
        <ExpandableNote label="Quest preparation" title="Make the correct amulet instead of enchanting it">
          <p>At <strong>24 Crafting</strong>, use <strong>one gold bar, one cut sapphire and an amulet mould</strong> at a furnace, then add a <strong>ball of wool</strong>. Hand in this <strong>strung sapphire amulet without enchanting it</strong>; an amulet of magic is not the requested item.</p>
          <p>For a missing bar buy gold ore from Ordan and smelt it; mine/cut a sapphire at Shilo until you have one. Buy the mould from Dommik in Al Kharid and shear/spin wool at Lumbridge, or buy a ball from Aemad in East Ardougne. Father Urhney replaces a ghostspeak amulet, and a spade spawns at the Falador estate agent.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-agility-70" number="23" title="Finish 70 Agility after the quest rewards">
        <p>Check your Agility level after Icthlarin's <strong>4,000 XP</strong>, training to 65 and Making Friends' <strong>50,000 XP</strong>. Continue the <strong>advanced Colossal Wyrm course</strong> as the lower-input default. Hallowed Sepulchre is an active alternative now that Sins is complete; use the floors available at your level. Stop at <strong>unboosted 70</strong>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-sailing-63" number="24" title="Sail to 63 and decide whether to build the Bosun's Bench">
        <p>Another short courier/charting/salvage return reaches <strong>unboosted 63 Sailing</strong>. With <strong>54 Construction</strong> already exceeded and the Red Reef schematic unlocked, the <strong>Bosun's workbench</strong> becomes available. Its recipe uses <strong>6 camphor planks, 24 adamantite nails and 5 lead bars</strong>, with a saw/hammer and the quest schematic. A crewmate assigned to it uses repair kits from the cargo hold to repair the boat automatically. You may wait until the adamantite-nail preparation after Smithing 70 below; do not grind rare salvage just to build it at 63. Build it only if you expect enough ship combat to value the automation; <strong>the workbench is optional</strong>. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Bosun%27s_workbench" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Facility recipe</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Finish the material-heavy gates</div><h2>Check your supplies and work in batches between Sailing trips.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i26-smithing-70" number="25" title="Finish 70 Smithing">
        <p>Check your Smithing XP now. The Red Reef's <strong>5,000 XP</strong> was claimed before training to 55, and Defender added another <strong>15,000 XP</strong> afterward. From exactly level 55 <em>before</em> Defender, its reward alone leaves about <strong>560,000 XP</strong> to level 70; any further Smithing reduces that amount. At Giants' Foundry, sword XP varies with alloy and performance, so check your <strong>remaining XP and banked bars</strong> before making more swords. Process ore from Motherlode Mine or other banked sources into bars; refill with ores/metal equipment only as needed. Ordinary anvil smithing is simpler; Blast Furnace gold plus goldsmith gauntlets is a faster, more active alternative if gold ore is available. Stop at <strong>unboosted 70</strong>; you can make the ship nails below with a boost instead of training to 74.</p>
        <p><strong>Make 300 adamantite nails for the skiff hull:</strong> the skiff hull needs <strong>300 adamantite nails</strong>, normally smithed at 74. At unboosted 70, buy <strong>two or three Kovac's grogs</strong> from the Giants' Foundry reward shop (<strong>300 reputation each</strong>; do a few commissions if you trained by another method). Each gives a reliable <strong>+4 Smithing</strong>; use the boost at an anvil to turn <strong>20 adamantite bars into 300 nails</strong> (15 per bar), redrinking before it decays. Smelt the bars at unboosted 70 from <strong>20 adamantite ores and 120 coal</strong> or use bars already banked. If you also want the optional workbench, budget <strong>two extra bars for 30 more nails</strong>; it uses 24. This lets you make the nails at 70 Smithing without waiting for drops or salvage. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Kovac%27s_grog" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Grog boost</a>.</p>
        <TrainingOptions id="i26-smithing-final-methods" informational={true} skill="Smithing" target="70, unboosted" why="Song of the Elves needs unboosted 70 Smithing; use a grog for the higher nail recipe." recommended="Giants' Foundry with your banked bars." relaxed="Ordinary smithing of banked bars." fast="Blast Furnace gold with goldsmith gauntlets if resources permit." />
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-sailing-67" number="26" title="Sail to 67 and fit a camphor hull to the skiff">
        <p>Resume from unboosted 63 with couriers, charting and salvage, checking your level between sessions. Stop at <strong>unboosted 67 Sailing</strong>: the camphor hull unlocked here prepares your boat for Chapter 3. The current <a href="https://umkyzn.github.io/BRUHsailer/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">BRUHsailer Chapter 3 boat plan</a> <strong>uses a camphor-hulled skiff</strong>, and this smaller boat keeps the material cost manageable. <strong>Check your boat first:</strong> the skiff purchase in 2.3 was optional, so if you are still using a raft, buy a <strong>skiff from a shipwright for 15,000 coins</strong> now; include that fee when checking how much cash you need. Cut <strong>50 camphor logs</strong> in the Red Reef's Sacred Grove and turn them into <strong>50 planks at a sawmill (2,500 coins per plank)</strong>. At a shipwright's workbench, make <strong>10 camphor hull parts</strong> (five planks per part); at the shipyard fit them to your <strong>skiff</strong> with the <strong>300 adamantite nails prepared above, 20 swamp tar and 5 lead bars</strong>. Collect any missing <strong>swamp tar from the ground in Lumbridge Swamp</strong>. If you have no lead banked, mine <strong>10 lead ores in Pandemonium Cave</strong> and smelt two ores per bar at a furnace; the 25 Mining/Smithing checks are already cleared. The hull requires <strong>67 Sailing and 59 Construction</strong>, both cleared. Check existing supplies before gathering; the skiff uses much less wood than a sloop's 16 large parts, which would take roughly 400 camphor planks. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Camphor_hull" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Boat-specific recipes</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-herblore-70" number="27" title="Use your banked herbs to finish 70 Herblore">
        <p>Before making more potions, check your Herblore XP after the rewards in 2.5, <strong>Sins' 90,000 XP</strong>, Tail's <strong>5,000</strong>, Fairytale II's <strong>3,500 + 2,500</strong>, Defender's museum <strong>5,000</strong>, Making History's <strong>1,000</strong>, and any potions you have already made. Starting at level 60 before Sins, those 2.6 rewards plus the tome provide <strong>107,000 XP</strong>, leaving roughly <strong>357,000 XP</strong> to level 70 before ordinary potion XP; you may need less if you started higher or have made more potions. Check your herbs and secondaries before deciding what to make. Make useful normal potions from accumulated kingdom and herb-run supplies as the lower-attention default, topping up with more runs/contracts while doing other route work if needed. Stop at <strong>unboosted 70</strong>.</p>
        <TrainingOptions id="i26-herblore-methods" informational={true} skill="Herblore" target="70, unboosted" why="Song of the Elves needs unboosted 70 Herblore. Check your XP and supplies between potion batches." recommended="Make potions the account will use from banked herbs and secondaries." resource="Mastering Mixology converts herbs to more XP per herb without ordinary secondaries, at higher attention." />
        <ExpandableNote label="Active, resource-efficient alternative" title="Mastering Mixology in Aldarin">
          <p>With <strong>unboosted 60 Herblore and Children of the Sun</strong> already complete, travel to <strong>Aldarin in Varlamore</strong> and enter the Alchemical Society's lab. Refine clean herbs or unfinished potions into <strong>Mox, Aga and Lye paste</strong>, load the hopper, mix the displayed ingredient combinations, process each potion at its indicated station, and hand in the requested orders for Herblore XP and resin. It extracts more XP per herb and avoids the normal potion secondaries, but is a more active loop than ordinary potion-making. Different herbs produce different paste; check the <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Mastering_Mixology" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">paste and order table</a> before refining valuable herbs. Stop when your Herblore reaches 70; no Mixology reward item is required.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <RouteStep id="i26-farming-70" number="28" title="Finish any remaining Farming levels to 70">
        <p>After a whole chapter of trees, fruit trees, Fossil hardwoods, herbs, Weiss and Farming Contracts, check the skill tab. If it already reads <strong>unboosted 70</strong>, you have finished this step. Otherwise use the seeds and runs you prefer. For a bounded <em>active</em> catch-up rather than waiting several more real-world days, go to <strong>Tithe Farm in Hosidius</strong> with a seed dibber, spade and watering cans. Take the highest seeds your unboosted Farming level permits (<strong>Bologano at 54</strong> until you qualify for a higher tier), plant, water and harvest in manageable batches, and repeat only until the measured XP gap closes. Skip Tithe Farm if your usual Farming runs have already brought you to 70. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Tithe_Farm" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Farm rules and seed tiers</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section id="chapter-complete" class="completion-panel">
        <div class="section-label">Before the elf quests · check unboosted levels</div>
        <h3>All eight Song of the Elves skills, without boosts.</h3>
        <table><thead><tr><th>Skill</th><th>Required unboosted level</th><th>How you reach it</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><td>Agility</td><td>70+</td><td>65 → Making Friends reward → final course</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Construction</td><td>70+</td><td>2.1 contracts + quest XP → Adept Homes</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Farming</td><td>70+</td><td>Background runs; Tithe Farm if short</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Herblore</td><td>70+</td><td>Quest lamps + potions or Mixology</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Hunter</td><td>70+</td><td>Eagles' Peak + Defender → rumours</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Mining</td><td>70+</td><td>Unboosted 71 for the earlier stout strategy</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Smithing</td><td>70+</td><td>Red Reef + Defender → Smithing</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Woodcutting</td><td>70+</td><td>Already unboosted 70 at Chapter 1 exit; no new grind</td></tr>
        </tbody></table>
        <p><strong>Also ready for the next chapter:</strong> unboosted <strong>60 Ranged</strong> and Ava's accumulator; unboosted <strong>67 Sailing</strong> and a camphor-hulled skiff; full Fairytale II; Icthlarin's Little Helper, A Tail of Two Cats, Dream Mentor, Making Friends/Weiss, Eagles' Peak, What Lies Below, Defender of Varrock, The Red Reef and Making History complete. The relevant Tail/Fairytale/Defender/Making History lamps went to Herblore. Check the eight listed skills without temporary boosts.</p>
        <p><strong>Continue to the elf quests in 2.7:</strong> Regicide → Roving Elves → Mourning's End Parts I/II → Song of the Elves. That page covers their items and boss preparation. Leave 56 Slayer and Path of Glouphrie, The Curse of Arrav and Sailing beyond 67 for Chapter 3.</p>
      </section>

